  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for climate and energy actitities in developing countries UNEP and UNEP-Ris&#xf8;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant consists of a core contribution (40 mio DKK) to UNEP DTU Partnership (a UNEP Collaborating Centre) Energy and Climate Collaboration and support (45 mio. DKK) to the Sustainable Energy for All (SE4ALL) Energy Efficiency Hub located in the UN-City in Copenhagen. The two interventions are key contributions to UNEP&#xbf;s Medium Term Strategy, 2014-17 and Programme of Work, addressing Climate Change and a priority to leverage the best science for the transformation towards renewable energy, energy efficiency and emission reductions. UNEP DTU Partnership and the Energy Efficiency Hub will at the global level help enable implementation of the global sustainable development goals and COP21 climate deal from Paris.

The UNEP DTU Partnership has country experience from work in around 70 countries. Currently, the Partnership is active in more than 50 developing countries; a number which is expected to increase. The increase is due to requests from more countries for technical support.</narrative>
  </description>
